    "title": "Until We Fall | Around The Web | wvnews.com",
    "text": "This has been a hard week in our country, from the school shooting in Denver, the assassination of Charlie Kirk, co-founder of Turning Point USA, and the 24th anniversary of the September 11 terrorist attack downing the north and south towers of the World Trade Center and taking the lives of 3,000 innocent people. All are evil, horrific acts that make no sense.\nBorn into sin ourselves, how can our first thoughts not be of vengeance and retribution? After all, we are a nation that professes the values of faith, freedom, and patriotism. We want to get even, to condemn not just the acts but the actors. Angry, we lash out. Afraid for our safety, we seek shelter lest we be harmed.",
